{"status":"answered","explanation":"The evidence details several actions Nero took to help the homeless following the fire.","claims": [{"text":"Nero threw open public spaces and buildings to the homeless as they were driven out, and he raised temporary structures for the destitute multitude.","citations":[{"id":"tacitus:39:1","path":"vault/raw/tacitus.html#681","quote":"However, to relieve the people, driven out homeless as they were, he threw open to them the Campus Martius and the public buildings of Agrippa, and even his own gardens, and raised temporary structures to receive the destitute multitude."}
]},{ "text":"Supplies of food were brought from Ostia and neighboring towns, and the price of corn was reduced to three sesterces a peck.","citations":[{"id":"tacitus:39:1","path":"vault/raw/tacitus.html#681","quote":"Supplies of food were brought up from Ostia and the neighbouring towns, and the price of corn was reduced to three sesterces a peck."}
]},{ "text":"Nero promised to erect colonnades at his own expense and to hand over open spaces to ground landlords once cleared of debris.","citations":[{"id":"tacitus:43:1","path":"vault/raw/tacitus.html#739","quote":"These colonnades Nero promised to erect at his own expense, and to hand over the open spaces, when cleared of the debris, to the ground landlords."}
]},{ "text":"Nero fixed on the marshes of Ostia for the reception of rubbish and arranged for ships bringing corn by the Tiber to sail down the river with cargoes of this rubbish.","citations":[{"id":"tacitus:43:1","path":"vault/raw/tacitus.html#739","quote":"He fixed on the marshes of Ostia for the reception of the rubbish, and arranged that the ships which had brought up corn by the Tiber, should sail down the river with cargoes of this rubbish."}
]}]}

